+#### ✅ Optional Configuration Preflight
+
+Before starting the CLI/UI or launching MCP servers, validate the local config,
+provider keys, core dependencies, workspace path, and MCP command availability:
+
+```bash
+python preflight_deepcode.py \
+  --config deepcode_config.json \
+  --output-json logs/preflight_deepcode.json \
+  --output-md logs/preflight_deepcode.md
+```
+
+Use `--strict` in CI to exit with a non-zero status when blockers are found. The
+preflight does not call LLM providers, install packages, start MCP servers, or
+launch Docker.
+
 #### 🤖 LLM Provider *(optional)*
 
 The provider is inferred from the `model` slug (`openai/...`, `anthropic/...`, `gemini/...`, etc.). To force a specific backend, set `agents.defaults.provider`:
diff --git a/preflight_deepcode.py b/preflight_deepcode.py
new file mode 100644
